#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Describes how long an IBM Quantum Compute Service job can run, regardless of what execution mode is used."
msgstr "Inilalarawan kung gaano katagal maaaring tumakbo ang isang IBM Quantum Compute Service job, anuman ang execution mode na ginagamit."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maximum execution time for IBM Quantum Compute Service workloads"
msgstr "Maximum execution time para sa mga IBM Quantum Compute Service workload"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To ensure fairness, there is a [service-enforced](#max-QPU) maximum amount of time each job can run. If a job exceeds this time limit, it is forcibly canceled and a `RuntimeJobMaxTimeoutError` exception is raised. You can also [set a maximum execution time](#max-job) on your jobs to help control costs.\n"
msgstr "Para masiguro ang pagiging patas, may [ipinatutupad ng serbisyo](#max-QPU) na maximum na tagal ng oras na maaaring tumakbo ang bawat job. Kung lalampas ang isang job sa limitasyong ito, ito ay puwersahang ika-kansela at itataas ang `RuntimeJobMaxTimeoutError` exception. Maaari ka ring [magtakda ng maximum execution time](#max-job) sa iyong mga job para makatulong sa pagkontrol ng gastos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   The session or batch is immediately terminated when the cost limit is reached. Any jobs currently running in that session or batch will run to completion, but any pending jobs will be canceled.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
" <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Ang session o batch ay agad na tinuturminate kapag naabot ang cost limit. Ang mga job na kasalukuyang tumatakbo sa session o batch na iyon ay patuloy na tatakbo hanggang sa matapos, ngunit ang anumang mga pending na job ay ika-kansela.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"max-job\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"max-job\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set a maximum execution time {#set-a-maximum-execution-time}"
msgstr "Magtakda ng maximum execution time {#set-a-maximum-execution-time}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum execution time for a job is the smaller of these values:\n"
msgstr "Ang maximum execution time para sa isang job ay ang pinakamaliit sa mga halagang ito:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The value set for `max_execution_time`\n"
msgstr "Ang halagang itinakda para sa `max_execution_time`\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The service's maximum timeout value (three hours)\n"
msgstr "Ang maximum na timeout value ng serbisyo (tatlong oras)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `max_execution_time` value is based on *QPU usage* (quantum usage only), not wall clock time.\n"
msgstr "Ang halaga ng `max_execution_time` ay batay sa *QPU usage* (quantum usage lamang), hindi sa wall clock time.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the maximum execution time (in seconds) on the job options, as shown in the following example.  See the [Estimator options](/guides/estimator-options), [Sampler options](/guides/sampler-options), or [Executor options](/guides/executor-options) guides for information about setting options.\n"
msgstr "Itakda ang maximum execution time (sa segundo) sa mga opsyon ng job, tulad ng ipinapakita sa sumusunod na halimbawa. Tingnan ang mga gabay na [Estimator options](/guides/estimator-options), [Sampler options](/guides/sampler-options), o [Executor options](/guides/executor-options) para sa impormasyon tungkol sa pagtatakda ng mga opsyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also find how much usage completed jobs have consumed by returning the job metrics as follows:\n"
msgstr "Maaari ka ring malaman kung gaano karaming usage ang nagamit ng mga natapos na job sa pamamagitan ng pagbabalik ng mga job metric tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"max-QPU\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"max-QPU\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Service-enforced maximum execution time {#service-enforced-maximum-execution-time}"
msgstr "Maximum execution time na ipinapatupad ng serbisyo {#service-enforced-maximum-execution-time}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The service enforces a maximum execution time limit of three hours to ensure fair device usage. If a `max_execution_time` is also specified for the job, the lesser of the two values is used.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapatupad ng serbisyo ang maximum na limitasyon sa execution time na tatlong oras upang matiyak ang patas na paggamit ng device. Kung may tinukoy ding `max_execution_time` para sa job, ginagamit ang mas maliit sa dalawang halaga.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, if you specify `max_execution_time=5000` (approximately 83 minutes), then the job is canceled after approximately 83 minutes, even though the service could allow it to run for three hours.\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa, kung itinakda mo ang `max_execution_time=5000` (humigit-kumulang 83 minuto), kanselado ang job pagkatapos ng humigit-kumulang 83 minuto, kahit na maaaring pahintulutan ito ng serbisyo na tumakbo nang tatlong oras.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"batch-max-time\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"batch-max-time\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batch maximum execution time {#batch-maximum-execution-time}"
msgstr "Maximum execution time ng Batch {#batch-maximum-execution-time}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a batch is started, it is assigned a maximum time to live (maximum TTL) value. After this TTL is reached, the batch is terminated, any jobs that are already running continue running, and any queued jobs that remain in the batch are put into a failed state.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nagsimula ang isang batch, ito ay itinalaga ng maximum time to live (maximum TTL) na halaga. Kapag naabot na ang TTL na ito, ang batch ay tinuturminate, ang mga job na tumatakbo na ay patuloy na tatakbo, at ang mga job na naka-queue pa sa batch ay ilalagay sa failed na estado.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batches also have an interactive time to live (interactive TTL) value between jobs that cannot be configured. If you don't explicitly close a batch, it is deactivated after the interactive TTL expires and can be reactivated at any time until it reaches its  maximum TTL.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga batch ay mayroon ding interactive time to live (interactive TTL) na halaga sa pagitan ng mga job na hindi maaaring i-configure. Kung hindi mo tahasang isasara ang isang batch, ito ay dide-deactivate pagkatapos ng interactive TTL at maaaring muling i-activate anumang oras hanggang maabot nito ang maximum TTL nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For instructions to work with these values, see [Run jobs in a batch](/guides/run-jobs-batch).\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga tagubilin sa pagtatrabaho sa mga halagang ito, tingnan ang [Run jobs in a batch](/guides/run-jobs-batch).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"session-max-time\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"session-max-time\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session maximum execution time {#session-maximum-execution-time}"
msgstr "Maximum execution time ng Session {#session-maximum-execution-time}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a session is started, it is assigned a maximum TTL value that determines how long a session can run. After this TTL is reached, the session is terminated, any jobs that are already running continue running, and any queued jobs that remain in the session are put into a failed state.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nagsimula ang isang session, ito ay itinalaga ng maximum TTL na halaga na nagtatakda kung gaano katagal maaaring tumakbo ang isang session. Kapag naabot na ang TTL na ito, ang session ay tinuturminate, ang mga job na tumatakbo na ay patuloy na tatakbo, at ang mga job na naka-queue pa sa session ay ilalagay sa failed na estado.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is also an interactive TTL value that cannot be configured.  If no session jobs are queued within that window, the session is temporarily deactivated.\n"
msgstr "Mayroon ding interactive TTL na halaga na hindi maaaring i-configure. Kung walang session job na naka-queue sa loob ng window na iyon, ang session ay pansamantalang dide-deactivate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For instructions to work with these values, see [Run jobs in a session](/guides/run-jobs-session).\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga tagubilin sa pagtatrabaho sa mga halagang ito, tingnan ang [Run jobs in a session](/guides/run-jobs-session).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other limitations {#other-limitations}"
msgstr "Iba pang mga limitasyon {#other-limitations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On the Open Plan, you can use up to 10 minutes on a QPU per 28-day rolling window. You can view an instance's usage on the [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) page.\n"
msgstr "Sa Open Plan, maaari kang gumamit ng hanggang 10 minuto sa isang QPU bawat 28-araw na rolling window. Maaari mong tingnan ang paggamit ng isang instance sa pahina ng [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances).\n"

